# Reproducer for the sva_rvfi_irq_valid_exclusive firings: the late shape of the timed-NMI knob
# Retained because rtl-arch's ruling record (gen_rvfi_irq_valid_exclusive_ruling.md) reads these runs, and
# they lived only under dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/wit/l32a, which is not a retained path.
# THE SHAPE: gen_knob_nmi_after_irq_delay = late, armed on the BRIDGE'S TAKEN EVENT, delay swept 1..8 per event.
#   The committed knob arms on the RAISE of a non-NMI line, as its own knob-table description states, so this
#   shape is reproduced by applying dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/gen_nmi_take_trigger.diff (sha256 first 12 8f54baec0b00),
#   two hunks in gen_irq_driver::run_phase moving the arm from the regime-event branch to the take-detection branch.
# THE BUILD: dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/wit/l32a, whose own compile log reports "sources sha256: cc08c9729184adc5".
#   That figure is the local runner's own, NOT the committer's gate digest; the shape was never committed, so no
#   gate identity exists for it and none is claimed.
# The run's own header, verbatim:
#   # run irq_nmi_late: 2026-09-04T16:16:34Z host=soc-l-11 seed=1 module=dv.auto_dv.gen_tb.gen_tests.gen_ut_lockstep build_sources_sha256=cc08c9729184adc5 plusargs=[+gen_mem_image=/tmp/claude-1211405897/-localdev-fzhang-ws-ibex-challenge/b61c04c6-06f1-4059-978d-29bc6123dadd/scratchpad/irqp/prog.vmem +gen_mem_image_crc32=8e882c5b +gen_mem_image_words=156 +gen_boot_addr=80000000 +gen_tohost_addr=800002d0 +gen_ut_boot_retire=2500 +gen_knob_irq_regime=storm +gen_knob_irq_line_mix=multi +gen_knob_nmi_after_irq_delay=late +gen_fetch_en_at_reset=0]

